a62e59e8e774023953e5cc152cd7adf70275e8641450f2ef2d8d6f", :author "wm-author", :entries {["futon-theory/progress-signal" 1] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/progress-signal" 1], :pattern "futon-theory/progress-signal", :pattern-sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/progress-signal", :objects {:G {:text "    - Evidence accumulation makes progress visible\n    - Metrics enable early intervention\n    - Health states trigger appropriate responses\n    - Dead mission detection prevents zombie work\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN evidence-accumulation ladder; the MAP-phase declaration is the target against which evidence must accumulate", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Ground the phase claim in accumulated evidence (criteria met, artifacts, decisions, sessions)"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You need to assess whether a mission is progressing, stalled, or dead.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Fragment 1 declares '**Status:** OPEN — MAP', a mission-phase statement; the pattern's IF is the need to assess whether a mission is progressing, stalled, or dead", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A mission whose phase must be read from its lifecycle state, not assumed"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Progress isn't always linear. Research phases may produce no artifacts.\n    Blocked missions may have zero commits but active waiting. The signal\n    must distinguish stalled from legitimately waiting.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: 'Progress isn't always linear... must distinguish stalled from legitimately waiting'; the fragment is a bare status line with no evidence attached yet", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Phase declaration alone is not progress: research and waiting phases can look stalled without being dead"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Track progress via evidence accumulation:\n\n    EVIDENCE-TYPES (in order of strength):\n    1. SUCCESS-CRITERIA-MET: Criterion checked off with proof\n    2. ARTIFACT-CREATED: Code, doc, test added (commit hash)\n    3. DECISION-MADE: Choice recorded in mission doc\n    4. BLOCKER-RESOLVED: Dependency cleared\n    5. REVIEW-COMPLETED: Milestone reviewed and approved\n    6. SESSION-LOGGED: PSR/PUR pair recorded (weakest signal)\n\n    PROGRESS-METRICS:\n    ```\n    velocity = evidence_count / time_elapsed\n    momentum = recent_evidence (last 7 days) / total_evidence\n    completion = criteria_met / total_criteria\n    ```\n\n    HEALTH-STATES:\n    - PROGRESSING: velocity > 0, momentum > 0.3\n    - SLOWING: velocity > 0, momentum < 0.3\n    - STALLED: velocity = 0 for > 7 days, not :blocked\n    - BLOCKED: explicitly marked :blocked with blocker\n    - DEAD: stalled > 30 days, no activity\n\n    INTERVENTION-TRIGGERS:\n    - SLOWING: Review scope, consider split\n    - STALLED: Diagnose cause, reassign or close\n    - DEAD: Archive with post-mortem\n\n    + COUNTER-RATCHET-FOR-MISSIONS:\n      Like code counts, mission evidence should not decrease:\n      - Criteria met stays met (unless scope changes)\n      - Artifacts created persist\n      - Sessions logged accumulate\n\n      If evidence decreases (reverted commit, criterion unmarked):\n      - Flag for investigation\n      - Require explicit justification\n\n    + VITALITY-INTEGRATION:\n      Mission progress feeds into stack vitality metrics:\n      - Active missions with evidence = healthy\n      - Many stalled missions = unhealthy\n      - High completion rate = velocity\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'Evidence accumulation makes progress visible... Dead mission detection prevents zombie work'", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Phase labels without evidence accumulate into zombie missions"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}, ["futon-theory/single-source-of-truth" 2] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/single-source-of-truth" 2], :pattern "futon-theory/single-source-of-truth", :pattern-sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/single-source-of-truth", :objects {:G {:text "    Identity is the foundation of relations. If entity A relates to entity B,\n    we must know exactly which entities those are. Ambiguity in identity\n    propagates to ambiguity in relations, making the entire graph unreliable.", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN explicit move on the named axis: steward the named substrate against the declared discipline", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Treat the named MiniLM-cosine pipeline as the single cited source for the analysis it anchors"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "The applicability scope of the pattern (see substructure).\n    + REQUIREMENTS:\n      - Every entity has exactly one UUID\n      - (source, external-id) tuple maps to exactly one UUID\n      - Duplicate external IDs rejected BEFORE write (not after)\n      - Lookups with ambiguous matches throw, never silently pick one\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Fragment 2 names 'the existing futon3a MiniLM-cosine' as substrate; pattern IF requires exactly one authoritative mapping per identity", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "One authoritative substrate must be named as the identity authority for a pipeline"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "The structural tension above manifests in the following concrete shapes (see substructure).\n    + FAILURE-MODES:\n      Duplicate external-id -> 409 (conflict)\n      Ambiguous lookup -> 409 (conflict)\n      Missing required identity -> 400 (bad request)\n\n    + ANTI-PATTERNS:\n      - Silently picking first match on ambiguous lookup\n      - Creating new UUID when external-id already exists\n      - Using external-id as UUID (they serve different purposes)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER failure-modes (duplicate/ambiguous identity) and anti-pattern 'silently picking first match'", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Naming a substrate does not settle whether it is the sole authority — ambiguity propagates if a second mapping source exists"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline.\n    + ENFORCEMENT:\n      Layer 1 validates before Layer 0 writes:\n      - Uniqueness check for existing (source, external-id) mapping\n      - On conflict: 409 with existing entity reference\n      - On ambiguous lookup: 409 with all matches listed\n\n    + DOMAIN-INSTANTIATION:\n      See `storage/identity-uniqueness` for concrete implementation patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'Ambiguity in identity propagates to ambiguity in relations'", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Identity ambiguity makes every downstream relation unreliable"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}, ["futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter" 3] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter" 3], :pattern "futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter", :pattern-sha256 "8015679fd94aa3063947311c48781b7ed1c6d2ed96083cef0b4e8926b22e306e", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter", :objects {:G {:text "      A metric is only trustworthy if truth can move it the \"wrong\" way; a counter that only ever goes\n      down is an incentive to conceal, not to do. (This is the operational face of earned-closure and\n      `[[aif/no-self-certification]]`.)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter.flexiarg", :sha256 "8015679fd94aa3063947311c48781b7ed1c6d2ed96083cef0b4e8926b22e306e"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN: 'make hidden work machine-VISIBLE — RAISE the hole-count... Accept the worse-looking number when it is the true one'; the fragment is that refusal enacted", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Raise the visible hole-count: label the pipeline output as artifact and refuse to count it as signal"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You can move a progress counter — check a box, close a mission, lower a count — to register progress.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter.flexiarg", :sha256 "8015679fd94aa3063947311c48781b7ed1c6d2ed96083cef0b4e8926b22e306e"}, :situation-source "Fragment 3 passes verdict '**artifact, not signal**' on the MiniLM-cosine pipeline; pattern IF is the moment a counter/measure can be moved to register progress", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A pipeline output is being judged: does it report reality or decorate it"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      If the counter UNDER-reports (the map shows fewer holes than the territory has) or the close is\n      UNEARNED (the field has not actually moved), the flattering move launders concealment as\n      progress. The map starts to flatter the territory, and the metric measures compliance, not reality.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter.flexiarg", :sha256 "8015679fd94aa3063947311c48781b7ed1c6d2ed96083cef0b4e8926b22e306e"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: 'If the counter UNDER-reports... the flattering move launders concealment as progress'; the fragment's 'artifact' verdict states this under-report", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The pipeline's output under-reports: it produces flattering decoration while the map flatters the territory"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Take the truthful move even against the counter: make hidden work machine-VISIBLE — RAISE the\n      hole-count — when the map under-reports; REFUSE the discharge — hold the close — when it is not\n      earned. Accept the worse-looking number when it is the true one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/honest-map-over-flattering-counter.flexiarg", :sha256 "8015679fd94aa3063947311c48781b7ed1c6d2ed96083cef0b4e8926b22e306e"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'a counter that only ever goes down is an incentive to conceal, not to do'", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A metric is only trustworthy if truth can move it the wrong way"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}, ["futon-theory/progress-signal" 5] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/progress-signal" 5], :pattern "futon-theory/progress-signal", :pattern-sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/progress-signal", :objects {:G {:text "    - Evidence accumulation makes progress visible\n    - Metrics enable early intervention\n    - Health states trigger appropriate responses\n    - Dead mission detection prevents zombie work\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN evidence-types include 'DECISION-MADE: Choice recorded in mission doc'; the declare-refocus fragment is that decision", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Record the refocus as an explicit DECISION-MADE evidence item so momentum metrics track the new focus, not the old one"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You need to assess whether a mission is progressing, stalled, or dead.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Fragment 5 announces 'centre of gravity has shifted'; pattern IF: assess whether a mission is progressing, stalled, or dead", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A mission's centre of gravity is being re-assessed mid-flight"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Progress isn't always linear. Research phases may produce no artifacts.\n    Blocked missions may have zero commits but active waiting. The signal\n    must distinguish stalled from legitimately waiting.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER on non-linear progress and the counter-ratchet ('If evidence decreases... flag for investigation')", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "A refocus can look like abandoning prior progress or conceal a stall unless it is declared with evidence"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Track progress via evidence accumulation:\n\n    EVIDENCE-TYPES (in order of strength):\n    1. SUCCESS-CRITERIA-MET: Criterion checked off with proof\n    2. ARTIFACT-CREATED: Code, doc, test added (commit hash)\n    3. DECISION-MADE: Choice recorded in mission doc\n    4. BLOCKER-RESOLVED: Dependency cleared\n    5. REVIEW-COMPLETED: Milestone reviewed and approved\n    6. SESSION-LOGGED: PSR/PUR pair recorded (weakest signal)\n\n    PROGRESS-METRICS:\n    ```\n    velocity = evidence_count / time_elapsed\n    momentum = recent_evidence (last 7 days) / total_evidence\n    completion = criteria_met / total_criteria\n    ```\n\n    HEALTH-STATES:\n    - PROGRESSING: velocity > 0, momentum > 0.3\n    - SLOWING: velocity > 0, momentum < 0.3\n    - STALLED: velocity = 0 for > 7 days, not :blocked\n    - BLOCKED: explicitly marked :blocked with blocker\n    - DEAD: stalled > 30 days, no activity\n\n    INTERVENTION-TRIGGERS:\n    - SLOWING: Review scope, consider split\n    - STALLED: Diagnose cause, reassign or close\n    - DEAD: Archive with post-mortem\n\n    + COUNTER-RATCHET-FOR-MISSIONS:\n      Like code counts, mission evidence should not decrease:\n      - Criteria met stays met (unless scope changes)\n      - Artifacts created persist\n      - Sessions logged accumulate\n\n      If evidence decreases (reverted commit, criterion unmarked):\n      - Flag for investigation\n      - Require explicit justification\n\n    + VITALITY-INTEGRATION:\n      Mission progress feeds into stack vitality metrics:\n      - Active missions with evidence = healthy\n      - Many stalled missions = unhealthy\n      - High completion rate = velocity\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/progress-signal.flexiarg", :sha256 "66407647b1ef3fe8a1cf196f3814cb170a3bf4c21a5fb5db362370971b9c36d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'Metrics enable early intervention... Health states trigger appropriate responses'", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Explicit decisions keep progress visible and trigger appropriate intervention on slowing or stalled states"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}, ["futon-theory/single-source-of-truth" 7] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/single-source-of-truth" 7], :pattern "futon-theory/single-source-of-truth", :pattern-sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/single-source-of-truth", :objects {:G {:text "    Identity is the foundation of relations. If entity A relates to entity B,\n    we must know exactly which entities those are. Ambiguity in identity\n    propagates to ambiguity in relations, making the entire graph unreliable.", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN: operate an explicit move on the named axis; the fragment names the replacement as the goal-state", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Commit to the single goal-state — the specified replacement — as the one authoritative target"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "The applicability scope of the pattern (see substructure).\n    + REQUIREMENTS:\n      - Every entity has exactly one UUID\n      - (source, external-id) tuple maps to exactly one UUID\n      - Duplicate external IDs rejected BEFORE write (not after)\n      - Lookups with ambiguous matches throw, never silently pick one\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Fragment 7 specifies the goal-state: '\"fix the biases\" to \"specify the goal-state and replace.'\"; pattern IF: one unambiguous identity per entity", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A substrate replacement must be specified as a definite goal-state identity, not a patch series"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "The structural tension above manifests in the following concrete shapes (see substructure).\n    + FAILURE-MODES:\n      Duplicate external-id -> 409 (conflict)\n      Ambiguous lookup -> 409 (conflict)\n      Missing required identity -> 400 (bad request)\n\n    + ANTI-PATTERNS:\n      - Silently picking first match on ambiguous lookup\n      - Creating new UUID when external-id already exists\n      - Using external-id as UUID (they serve different purposes)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER anti-patterns: creating a new identity when one already exists, or silently picking between ambiguous matches", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Two candidate authorities (patching the old substrate vs a specified replacement) create identity ambiguity about what the system will be"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "Operate an explicit move on the named axis (see substructure below); steward the pattern against the declared discipline.\n    + ENFORCEMENT:\n      Layer 1 validates before Layer 0 writes:\n      - Uniqueness check for existing (source, external-id) mapping\n      - On conflict: 409 with existing entity reference\n      - On ambiguous lookup: 409 with all matches listed\n\n    + DOMAIN-INSTANTIATION:\n      See `storage/identity-uniqueness` for concrete implementation patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/single-source-of-truth.flexiarg", :sha256 "451614d5456b62248039f366e293bfe6bd703475b48a4c3ed019305c983f7270"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: identity is the foundation of relations; ambiguity makes the entire graph unreliable", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Without one committed goal-state, ambiguity propagates into every downstream relation and plan"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}, ["futon-theory/mission-dependency" 7] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/mission-dependency" 7], :pattern "futon-theory/mission-dependency", :pattern-sha256 "1805ee0861f02b1cb198be733bc09c1b9067b6339ca13b24cdadf5e547fd653a", :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/mission-dependency", :objects {:G {:text "    - Explicit dependencies prevent wasted work on blocked missions\n    - Graph structure enables priority inference\n    - Unblock propagation accelerates overall progress\n    - Shared resources surface coordination needs\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-dependency.flexiarg", :sha256 "1805ee0861f02b1cb198be733bc09c1b9067b6339ca13b24cdadf5e547fd653a"}, :situation-source "Pattern THEN DAG modeling with relationship types; the fragment's specify-and-replace decision is the node whose edges must be recorded", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Model the replacement goal-state as an explicit node with blocks/enables/shares edges to affected missions"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You are planning work across multiple missions or diagnosing why\n    a mission is stuck.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-dependency.flexiarg", :sha256 "1805ee0861f02b1cb198be733bc09c1b9067b6339ca13b24cdadf5e547fd653a"}, :situation-source "Fragment 7's goal-state shift is planning-level; pattern IF: 'planning work across multiple missions'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Planning work whose goal-state change restructures what other missions depend on"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Dependencies can be circular (requiring negotiation), soft (preferred\n    but not required), or discovered late. The graph must be maintainable.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-dependency.flexiarg", :sha256 "1805ee0861f02b1cb198be733bc09c1b9067b6339ca13b24cdadf5e547fd653a"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: 'Dependencies can be circular... soft... or discovered late'", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Dependencies may be soft, circular, or discovered late as the goal-state shifts"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Model missions as a directed acyclic graph (DAG):\n\n    RELATIONSHIP-TYPES:\n    - blocks: Mission A must complete before Mission B can start\n    - enables: Mission A completion makes Mission B easier (soft)\n    - shares: Missions A and B share a resource or decision\n    - parent-child: Mission A spawned Mission B (split)\n\n    REPRESENTATION:\n    In mission docs:\n    ```\n    Blocked-by: M-other-mission.md\n    Enables: M-downstream.md\n    ```\n\n    CONSTRAINTS:\n    - No orphan missions (every mission linked to at least one other or to root)\n    - No cycles in \"blocks\" relationships\n    - Blocked missions must cite specific blocker\n    - When blocker completes, blocked mission notified\n\n    PRIORITY-INFERENCE:\n    - Missions that unblock many others have higher priority\n    - Leaf missions (no blockers) can proceed immediately\n    - Root missions (no dependents) may be deprioritized\n\n    + VISUALIZATION:\n      The mission graph can be rendered:\n      ```\n      M-futon1a-rebuild\n          ├── blocks → M-futon1a-migration\n          └── enables → M-pattern-inference-engine\n\n      M-make-agency-work-properly\n          └── blocks → M-codex-parity\n      ```\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-dependency.flexiarg", :sha256 "1805ee0861f02b1cb198be733bc09c1b9067b6339ca13b24cdadf5e547fd653a"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: 'Explicit dependencies prevent wasted work on blocked missions... Unblock propagation accelerates overall progress'", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Explicit dependency edges prevent wasted work on missions implicitly blocked by the substrate replacement"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}}}, :voids {["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 0] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 0], :pattern "futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation", :missing-parts [:IF :HOWEVER], :reason :pattern-part-missing}, ["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 3] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 3], :pattern "futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation", :missing-parts [:IF :HOWEVER], :reason :pattern-part-missing}, ["futon-theory/task-as-arrow" 4] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/task-as-arrow" 4], :pattern "futon-theory/task-as-arrow", :missing-parts [:IF :HOWEVER], :reason :pattern-part-missing}, ["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 6] {:occurrence-id ["futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation" 6], :pattern "futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation", :missing-parts [:IF :HOWEVER], :reason :pattern-part-missing}}, :schema :wm/occurrence-square-registry-v1, :digest "f9d2f590435d806f3e2073d169e8b0d9ca9cb59bcfe80048c5fdcf2c09420159"}}